1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,899
This is Priya.

2
00:00:00,899 --> 00:00:04,302
Someone in her family is ready to leave the hospital.

3
00:00:04,302 --> 00:00:08,477
But discharge is stuck on one phrase: insurance approval pending.

4
00:00:08,477 --> 00:00:09,890
She needs two answers.

5
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:13,044
Can we leave, and what do we still owe?

6
00:00:13,044 --> 00:00:18,619
She opens Claim911, explains the problem once, and allows it to investigate.

7
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:23,231
Let’s follow what happens next in this synthetic case.

8
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:30,619
They told us final insurance clearance is pending, but we don’t know which approval or document is

9
00:00:30,619 --> 00:00:31,223
missing.

10
00:00:31,223 --> 00:00:38,131
We are ready to leave and need Claim911 to check with the hospital and the insurer.

11
00:00:38,131 --> 00:00:44,776
First, Claim911 calls the hospital insurance desk, then the claims administrator, or TPA.

12
00:00:44,776 --> 00:00:51,944
The TPA needs three documents, and an existing request for additional cover has not been linked.

13
00:00:51,944 --> 00:00:56,551
An earlier approval is not final discharge clearance.

14
00:00:56,551 --> 00:00:58,995
There are three owners to coordinate.

15
00:00:58,995 --> 00:01:01,042
Billing has the corrected bill.

16
00:01:01,042 --> 00:01:03,948
Medical records holds the discharge summary.

17
00:01:03,948 --> 00:01:06,193
The implant store has the invoice.

18
00:01:06,193 --> 00:01:13,116
Priya can also upload receipts herself; the portal keeps uploaded and verified states separate.

19
00:01:13,117 --> 00:01:18,823
Claim911 asks medical records: is the discharge summary signed?

20
00:01:18,823 --> 00:01:24,211
No, the discharge summary is awaiting the treating team’s signature.

21
00:01:24,211 --> 00:01:29,774
Claim911 keeps the unsigned summary pending and follows up with medical records.

22
00:01:29,774 --> 00:01:33,947
Later, the signed version is released, uploaded and checked.

23
00:01:33,947 --> 00:01:40,648
Together with the corrected bill and implant invoice, the response packet is now ready.

24
00:01:40,648 --> 00:01:46,087
Now Priya sees exactly what will be shared, with whom, and which versions.

25
00:01:46,087 --> 00:01:47,925
She approves that packet.

26
00:01:47,925 --> 00:01:51,380
If a document changes, Claim911 must ask again.

27
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:54,823
It can now ask the hospital to submit.

28
00:01:54,823 --> 00:02:00,789
Hi, this is Claim911 calling about final request F, I, N, six, three.

29
00:02:00,789 --> 00:02:04,595
Can you submit the approved response packet?

30
00:02:04,845 --> 00:02:09,389
The approved response packet has been dispatched.

31
00:02:09,389 --> 00:02:12,606
Dispatch reference HSP01.

32
00:02:12,356 --> 00:02:13,910
Sent is not received.

33
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:19,534
Claim911 checks the TPA’s receiving-side record against the approved packet.

34
00:02:19,534 --> 00:02:28,324
Receipt is confirmed, but the claim is still pending: the query and additional-cover request must be resolved.

35
00:02:28,324 --> 00:02:29,064
Understood.

36
00:02:29,064 --> 00:02:35,597
Please resolve the query and link the existing enhancement E, N, H, one, eight using the received

37
00:02:35,597 --> 00:02:37,214
response in your system.

38
00:02:37,214 --> 00:02:40,784
Could you tell me the actual result after doing this?

39
00:02:41,034 --> 00:02:49,234
ENH18 is now linked and the query is marked answered, with the claim decision still pending.

40
00:02:48,984 --> 00:02:55,528
With the query answered and the additional cover linked, the insurer issues an authorization.

41
00:02:55,528 --> 00:03:02,354
The hospital then reconciles the bill and deposit, and issues administrative discharge clearance.

42
00:03:02,354 --> 00:03:06,594
Only now can Claim911 give Priya a verified answer.

43
00:03:06,593 --> 00:03:12,146
The hospital confirmed your discharge and issued a final bill of INR 248,000.

44
00:03:12,146 --> 00:03:15,319
The insurer approved payment of INR 230,000.

45
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:17,122
Your share is INR 18,000.

46
00:03:17,122 --> 00:03:21,521
You paid a deposit of INR 30,000, so the balance due is zero.

47
00:03:21,521 --> 00:03:26,209
The refund due is INR 12,000 but it is not yet confirmed as paid.

48
00:03:26,209 --> 00:03:29,815
Shall I explain the billing details next?

49
00:03:29,816 --> 00:03:32,159
Here is what changed for the family.

50
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:33,852
No balance remains to pay.

51
00:03:33,852 --> 00:03:36,131
Twelve thousand rupees is due back.

52
00:03:36,131 --> 00:03:42,967
The portal shows the supporting sources, and keeps refund payment open until there is evidence.

53
00:03:42,967 --> 00:03:48,107
That is Claim911: Bolna conversations connected to a controlled workflow.

54
00:03:48,107 --> 00:03:55,290
It finds the blocker, coordinates the people and documents, asks permission, and verifies the outcome.

55
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:58,828
So families can focus on their loved one.
